--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reviewed before packaging, as required by OD-05:

  - Skilit original code under Apache-2.0 combined with MIT-licensed
    runtime dependencies (§6): COMPATIBLE. MIT permits sublicensing
    under Apache-2.0 terms for the combined work; no relicensing of
    the MIT components is claimed — their notices are preserved via
    this file and their own license texts travel with the packages.
  - Apache-2.0 runtime dependencies (PGlite, Playwright-core): SAME
    LICENSE family, no conflict.
  - ISC-licensed pg-int8 (transitive): permissive, compatible.
  - MPL-2.0 axe-core 4.14.0: dev-only transitive (via
    eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y in the lint chain). NOT distributed in the
    runtime candidate (node_modules are excluded from the source
    tarball; dependencies arrive via the frozen lockfile at install
    time). No MPL-licensed file is modified or bundled. NO CONFLICT
    for this distribution; recorded here for completeness.
  - Fair Source WIP (artcraft-services): restrictive and NOT an
    open-source grant. No services file is distributed; reuse, if ever
    activated, rides solely on the founder authorization for narrow
    paths. NO CONFLICT because no restricted file ships.
  - monet-registry files (§2): upstream license unverified; distributed
    SOLELY under the recorded founder authorization, carved out of the
    Apache-2.0 grant. NO RELICENSING is claimed. NO CONFLICT provided
    this carve-out is preserved in redistribution.
  - Inter Tight 600 wordmark font, SIL OFL 1.1 (§7a): the candidate DOES
    bundle a reduced Latin WOFF2 subset and OFL-derived wordmark outline
    geometry, so this finding was redone for that distribution. SIL OFL
    1.1 grants unrestricted use, bundling, modification and redistribution
    provided the copyright notice and the license text travel with the
    font and the Modified Version remains under this license. The upstream
    notice ("Copyright 2022 The Inter Project Authors", immutable pin
    fac60545cc0de9d4eff6eb5b1ab88bcdfc9ecc69) specifies no Reserved Font
    Name, so the OFL rename restriction does not apply; the webfont is
    nonetheless distributed under the distinct family name "Inter Tight
    Skilit" so that a modified subset is not presented as the upstream
    family. The OFL text ships with the font
    (docs/brand/licenses/Inter-Tight-OFL.txt), the outline geometry is
    recorded as an OFL-governed derivative, and the font name is used
    descriptively only (trademarks remain excluded, §10). NO CONFLICT.
  - Restricted third-party assets, weights, services, brands (§7–§9):
    EXCLUDED from the candidate, apart from the Inter Tight subset
    recorded in §7a. NO CONFLICT.

Result: no genuine licensing conflict blocks this source-release
